    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d600">

                <pb facs="0896" n="886" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg886"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.93/11–2946: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-11-29T15:00:00+08:00">November 29,
                            1946—3 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:06 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1996. For the Acting Secretary. I wish you to know that I believe it to be of the
                    utmost importance that General Marshall’s plan for withdrawal of some 10,000
                    Marines in two installments be undertaken with the least possible delay, and I
                    hope that you are in full accord with this view and will assist in its
                    implementation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
